* Small-signal model of the PMOS common-source stage with cascoded NMOS current-source load (all devices saturated)
Vin in 0 {v_in}
* M3: PMOS input device, source at AC ground (VDD); current gm3*v_sg3 flows into out, v_sg3 = -v_in
G3 0 out 0 in {gm3}
RO3 out 0 {r_O3}
* M2: cascode, gate at AC ground (Vb1), source at X, bulk at ground: v_gs2 = v_bs2 = -v_X
Gm2 out X 0 X {gm2}
Gmb2 out X 0 X {gmb2}
RO2 out X {r_O2}
* M1: gate at Vb2 (AC ground), only its output resistance remains
RO1 X 0 {r_O1}
.end
